      "summary": "The tasks panel shows progress and results for operations that do not finish immediately.",
      "html": "<h2>Who can perform the operation</h2>\n<p>A job is visible to the user who started the operation and can access the module.</p>\n<h2>Where to find the feature</h2>\n<p>Use the tasks button in the application header after starting a bulk operation or derivative generation.</p>\n<h2>How to perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Open the panel, find the job by type and start time, then review success and error counts. If the job produced a file, use the result download action.</p>\n<h2>Result</h2>\n<p>Status changes in real time. A completed run retains its summary and, where applicable, a link to its artifact.</p>\n<h2>Limitations and special cases</h2>\n<p>One failed item does not necessarily fail the whole job. File links can expire and are generated again when requested.</p>\n<h2>Related topics</h2>\n<p>Jobs are created by <a href=\"/catalog/documentation/products-bulk-edit\">Bulk editing</a> and the <a href=\"/catalog/documentation/multimedia-library\">Media library</a>, among other features.</p>\n",
