      "html": "<h2>Who can perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Every Catalog user can perform basic diagnostics; changing permissions requires an administrator.</p>\n<h2>Where to find the feature</h2>\n<p>Check the on-screen message, toast, and job details in the header tasks panel.</p>\n<h2>How to perform the operation</h2>\n<p>Verify the active filter and selection, refresh the list, and check whether a file is referenced by a product. For access denial, compare the requirement with the permissions article.</p>\n<h2>Result</h2>\n<p>After removing the cause, the operation can be retried without manually clearing local application state.</p>\n<h2>Limitations and special cases</h2>\n<p>Do not repeatedly submit a job that is still running. Partial success requires reviewing failed items, not reversing successful ones.</p>\n<h2>Related topics</h2>\n<p>See <a href=\"/catalog/documentation/permissions\">Permissions</a> and <a href=\"/catalog/documentation/background-jobs\">Background jobs</a>.</p>\n",
